# el++ engine fixture 31 (src/test.slop: ksc-fixture-at, test-ksc-entailments).
# 31. Rule (28) through holders, irreplaceably. Every member of {a}
# derives a's own classes itself ({a} ⊑ A is a GCI), so (28) is
# needed only for a class that reaches a from another member by
# (27). Witness w2 of c holds {a} at round 3 (C(c), C ⊑ ∃r.D,
# D ⊑ {a}); witness w1 of e holds Z at round 2 and {a} only at
# round 4 (E(e), E ⊑ ∃s.F0, F0 ⊑ Z, F0 ⊑ F1, F1 ⊑ {a}). Z reaches
# a by (27) after w2's {a} was processed, so inst(w2, Z) is in G
# only through (28) over holders(a); the stored-G test compares it.
# Inside el++ whole: the engine must answer every class as the literal Psc
# reference does (test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).

@prefix : <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty . :t a owl:ObjectProperty .
:C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual .
:E a owl:Class . :F0 a owl:Class . :F1 a owl:Class . :Z a owl:Class .
:c a owl:NamedIndividual , :C .
:e a owl:NamedIndividual , :E .
:C rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :D ] .
:D rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:oneOf ( :a ) ] .
:E rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:someValuesFrom :F0 ] .
:F0 rdfs:subClassOf :Z , :F1 .
:F1 rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:oneOf ( :a ) ] .
